# 2000-04-18  "Harmonic Convergence" (dave)
#
#   harmonics.world was created by the merger of the original
#   harmonics file, harmonics.canadian, harmonics.japan, and
#   harmonics.admiralty.  The merger was technically made possible
#   just by me deciding that some of the things that Jean-Pierre
#   LaPointe and Toru Suzuki did were probably by mistake and giving
#   up on trying to understand and reproduce them.  The business case
#   for doing the merger in and of itself is easier and more
#   consistent data maintenance.  But in addition, the extension of
#   congen to approximate Doodson formulated constituents and the
#   availability of new expertise enabled me to add the constituents
#   needed to import data that did not fit into any of the previous
#   harmonics files.  Henceforth, it will be pretty easy to add
#   constituents as needed without a proliferation of incompatible
#   harmonics files.
#
#   Sorry about the size :-/  I never expected to have so many
#   constituents, so XTide doesn't handle sparse data sets
#   efficiently.
#
#   The location names from harmonics.canadian and harmonics.japan
#   were processed to make them mesh with the canonical naming system.
#   Canadian locations were automagically placed into provinces;
#   doubtless there are errors.  Still to do:  fix aliasing of
#   locations, search for typo sets, and import the remaining old
#   data.
#
#   Nits that were fixed during the import and merge:
#   1.  In harmonics.admiralty, Skua Well No 4 had the same constituents
#       as Thevenard Island.  Deleted both.
#   2.  In harmonics.canadian, the same thing happened withth Roberts Bank,
#       Washington and Tsawwassen, British Columbia.
#   3.  Revised some probably incorrect time zones in harmonics.canadian.
#
#   Please refer to the commentary in the file harmonics.world.condata
#   in the distribution condata.tar.gz in the XTide FTP directory for
#   explanation of some of the constituents and details of what changed
#   for Canada and Japan data.
